---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---

<DocsLayout title="Kubernetes">
  <h1>Kubernetes</h1>
  <p>
    Identity is a single stateless container; the Kubernetes object set is
    minimal. This page is a reference manifest you can adapt — there is
    no Helm chart in the repo, intentionally.
  </p>

  <h2>Secret</h2>
  <p>The JWT key ring and TOTP encryption key belong in a Secret:</p>
  <Code code={`apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: identity-secrets
  namespace: identity
type: Opaque
stringData:
  GATEWAY_JWT_KEYS: |
    [{"kid":"k-2026-05","private_key_pem":"-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\\n...\\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\\n","active":true}]
  GATEWAY_TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY: "<base64 32-byte key>"
  GATEWAY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET: "..."
  GATEWAY_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET: "..."`} lang="yaml" title="secret.yaml" />

  <h2>ConfigMap</h2>
  <Code code={`apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: identity-config
  namespace: identity
data:
  GATEWAY_ENTDB_ADDRESS: "entdb.entdb.svc.cluster.local:50051"
  GATEWAY_DEFAULT_TENANT_ID: "acme"
  GATEWAY_PASSKEY_RP_ID: "acme.example.com"
  GATEWAY_PASSKEY_ORIGIN: "https://acme.example.com"
  GATEWAY_TOTP_ISSUER: "Acme"
  GATEWAY_ALLOWED_ORIGINS: "https://acme.example.com"
  GATEWAY_AUTH_ALLOW_LOCAL: "true"
  GATEWAY_COOKIE_SECURE: "true"
  GATEWAY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID: "..."
  GATEWAY_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID: "..."`} lang="yaml" title="configmap.yaml" />

  <h2>Deployment</h2>
  <Code code={`apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: identity
  namespace: identity
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels: { app: identity }
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: { app: identity }
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: identity
          image: ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0
          ports:
            - { containerPort: 80, name: http }
            - { containerPort: 9090, name: metrics }
          envFrom:
            - configMapRef: { name: identity-config }
            - secretRef:    { name: identity-secrets }
          readinessProbe:
            httpGet: { path: /healthz, port: 80 }
            periodSeconds: 5
          livenessProbe:
            httpGet: { path: /healthz, port: 80 }
            periodSeconds: 10
          resources:
            requests: { cpu: "100m", memory: "128Mi" }
            limits:   { cpu: "500m", memory: "256Mi" }
          securityContext:
            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
            runAsNonRoot: true
            capabilities:
              drop: ["ALL"]`} lang="yaml" title="deployment.yaml" />

  <h2>Service</h2>
  <Code code={`apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: identity
  namespace: identity
  labels: { app: identity }
spec:
  selector: { app: identity }
  ports:
    - { name: http,    port: 80,   targetPort: http }
    - { name: metrics, port: 9090, targetPort: metrics }`} lang="yaml" title="service.yaml" />

  <h2>Scaling</h2>
  <p>
    The container is stateless — replicas are interchangeable. A single
    <code>Deployment</code> with 2-3 replicas behind a <code>Service</code>
    is sufficient for typical workloads. Vertical capacity is bounded by
    bcrypt: at cost 12, a single core can hash about 4 passwords per
    second. If signup rate is bursty, consider an HPA on CPU.
  </p>

  <h2>Pod Disruption Budget</h2>
  <Code code={`apiVersion: policy/v1
kind: PodDisruptionBudget
metadata:
  name: identity
  namespace: identity
spec:
  minAvailable: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels: { app: identity }`} lang="yaml" />

  <h2>Ingress</h2>
  <p>
    Use whatever ingress the cluster has. The relevant facts:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Identity speaks HTTP/1.1 + HTTP/2 cleartext on <code>:80</code>.</li>
    <li>The path namespace is <code>/identity.IdentityService/*</code> and <code>/.well-known/jwks.json</code> + <code>/health*</code>.</li>
    <li>Make sure the ingress preserves <code>Host</code> + <code>Origin</code> headers — Connect uses them, and CORS / passkey RP-ID checks depend on them.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
